                        tags$em("plus X kb on each side"), " \u2014 so \u00b110 kb means 10 kb upstream ", tags$em("and"), " 10 kb downstream, totalling gene\u00a0+\u00a020\u00a0kb of context."
                    ),
                    tags$li(
                        tags$strong("Gene body shading"), ": the light blue-grey background covers exactly the transcribed region of the reference gene. Regions outside this shading (left and right edges when a flank is selected) are the flanking intergenic context \u2014 biologically relevant for identifying conserved non-coding elements, promoters, and enhancers."
                    ),
                    tags$li(tags$strong("Gene structure panel (top)"), ": displays the reference gene annotation \u2014 CDS blocks (numbered from 5\u2032 to 3\u2032), UTR regions, the intron backbone, and strand-direction arrows. Exon numbers follow transcription order: exon 1 is nearest the transcription start site."),
                    tags$li(tags$strong("Y-axis within each query row"), ": vertical position of each gap-free segment encodes its percent sequence identity to the reference (50% at bottom, 100% at top). This is the PipMaker / PipAlign convention."),
                    tags$li(tags$strong("Vertical CDS / UTR bands"), ": the coloured vertical shading marks where coding exons (CDS) and UTR regions fall along the x-axis. Segments aligning within these bands have direct coding or regulatory relevance."),
